---
import StoryHero from './StoryHero.astro';
import StoryChapter from './StoryChapter.astro';
import StoryFocus from './StoryFocus.astro';
import StoryLearnings from './StoryLearnings.astro';
import ProjectMedia from './ProjectMedia.astro';
import latestMedia from '../../data/hanji-media.json';
import HanjiWalkthrough from './HanjiWalkthrough.astro';
import type { WorkEntry, ProjectEvidence } from '../../data/work';
interface Props { work: WorkEntry }
const { work } = Astro.props;
const evidence = work.project?.sections.flatMap(section => section.visuals?.flatMap(visual => visual.media ?? []) ?? []) ?? [];
function media(src: string, caption: string, displayWidth = 1200): ProjectEvidence {
  const item = [...latestMedia, ...evidence].find(item => item.src === src);
  if (!item) throw new Error(`Hanji evidence missing: ${src}`);
  return { ...item, caption, displayWidth, description: undefined } as ProjectEvidence;
}
---
<article class="hanji-story">
  <StoryHero title="A place to think, direct and judge agent work."
    intro="Agents made it easier to produce more. I built Hanji to make that work easier to understand: explore an idea, shape a plan, and keep the decisions readable."
    links={[{label:'Visit Hanji',url:'https://hanji.ink/'}]}>
    <Fragment slot="title">More ways to make.<br />A clearer place<br /><em>to decide.</em></Fragment>
    <figure slot="visual" class="opening-visual">
      <img src="/work/hanji/flow-think-board.webp" width="1440" height="1000" alt="Hanji Think with notes exploring a simpler first week for a new team" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" />
      <figcaption>Think: give the question room before it becomes a task.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </StoryHero>
  <div class="hanji-journey">
    <StoryChapter id="hanji-foundations" class="hanji-chapter" title={'My work.\nMy data.'} intro="One of my first decisions was that the data should remain mine. I wanted control over the work I put into Hanji, including how I could keep it, inspect it and carry it elsewhere.">
      <p class="foundation-copy">That led me to build around Git, a version-control system for files and their history. Data ownership was a starting requirement: the interface could evolve around my work without becoming the only way to access it.</p>
      <p class="foundation-copy">The other starting point was my daily use of large language models (LLMs). I wanted an interface that could give them the full context of the work I was doing, so I could direct them without repeatedly reconstructing that context in a separate conversation.</p>
    </StoryChapter>
    <StoryChapter id="hanji-flow" class="hanji-chapter" title={'One workspace.\nFollow the work through it.'} intro="Hanji brings together Think, a canvas for exploration; Plan, a place to organize and direct tasks; and Document, a shared reading and editing surface. This example follows a small design question: how can a new team reach its first shared board sooner?">
      <HanjiWalkthrough />
    </StoryChapter>
    <StoryChapter id="hanji-context" class="hanji-chapter" title={'The hard part was not making more.\nIt was keeping the reasoning intact.'} intro="I began with documents that agents could already read and change. People needed an equally useful place to question them. Document came first, then Plan for directing execution, then Think for the exploration before either.">
      <StoryFocus topic="Keeping the context" problem="A sketch, a task and a document serve different purposes. Moving between them should not mean starting the explanation again.">
        <div class="detail-spread">
          <div class="detail-copy"><h3>Give the next action<br />a reason to exist.</h3><p>In Think, a note can become an issue, and a selection can become a page. A passage in Document can become a task with its quotation attached. The source matters as much as the destination.</p><p>These connections are implemented locally and still being tested together. I want the person taking over the work to understand why it exists, not just what to do.</p></div>
          <ProjectMedia media={media('/work/hanji/flow-document-read.webp','The brief keeps the evidence, decision and open question together.',800)} />
        </div>
      </StoryFocus>
    </StoryChapter>
    <StoryChapter id="hanji-direction" class="hanji-chapter" title={'Direction belongs\nbeside the work.'} intro="The conductor is the shared agent control across the workspace. It gives me a place to direct the broader effort; comments on a specific task let me give precise instructions and follow the response beside the work.">
      <p class="foundation-copy">I tried terminals, then a separate in-app conversation. Each created another place to follow and another context to maintain. Bringing the exchange into the task keeps its brief, discussion and next decision together. That is the interface I needed for the models I was already using every day.</p>
      <ProjectMedia media={media('/work/hanji/flow-plan-issue.webp','An issue brings its brief, related work and discussion into one view.')} />
    </StoryChapter>
    <StoryChapter id="hanji-design" class="hanji-chapter" title={'Care shows up\nin the repeated actions.'} intro="I use Document and Plan at Buzzvil every day. That makes small interruptions hard to ignore: losing a reading position, rebuilding a board to open an issue, or leaving a canvas to manage a discussion.">
      <div class="detail-spread">
        <div class="detail-copy"><h3>Keep the surface steady.<br />Let the work change.</h3><p>Reading and editing share a page. Opening an issue preserves the board behind it. On the canvas, voting and the timer open beside the ideas under discussion.</p><p>Think, Plan and Document now share neutral surfaces, a workspace accent and familiar navigation. The consistency is useful because the task changes more often than the person’s intent.</p></div>
        <ProjectMedia media={media('/work/hanji/think-voting.webp','A voting session stays next to the ideas it helps the group choose.',800)} />
      </div>
    </StoryChapter>
  </div>
  <StoryLearnings title={'What I learned:\nuse it to understand it.'}>
    <p>The useful unit is not a screen or an agent conversation. It is a decision with enough context for someone to understand it, question it and carry it forward.</p>
    <p>Hanji is still early. Document is being tested privately; Plan and Think are development previews. Think supports live rich-text editing in a single-server workspace, without remote synchronization. Public desktop downloads are not yet available.</p>
    <p>Dogfooding, using the product for my own daily work, has been essential. Hanji grew out of my needs and habits. Whenever an interaction felt awkward or interrupted my flow, I went back and changed it. Living with the tool revealed friction I had missed while designing and building it.</p>
    <p>That made the value of daily use especially clear at this early stage: small moments of discomfort can shape the product before they become established patterns. My own workflow is the starting point. The next step is to learn which decisions hold up in other people’s work.</p>
  </StoryLearnings>
</article>

<style>
  .foundation-copy { max-width:62ch;margin:1.5rem auto; }
  .hanji-story { --hanji-celadon: #1e8485; --hanji-orchid: #8d43b8; font-family: var(--story-body, sans-serif); min-width: 0; }
  .hanji-story a { color: inherit; text-underline-offset: 5px; }
  .hanji-story a:focus-visible, summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid currentColor; outline-offset: 5px; }
  .hanji-story em { font: inherit; font-style: italic; color: #c6c6bc; }
  .opening-visual { min-width: 0; margin: 0; }
  .opening-visual figcaption { margin-top: .75rem; font: .75rem/1.6 var(--story-body); color: #b8bbb1; }
  .opening-visual img { display: block; width: 100%; height: auto; border: 1px solid #44473d; border-radius: 5px; }
  .hanji-story h3 { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; font: 400 clamp(1.85rem, 2.6vw, 2.65rem)/1.15 var(--story-display, Georgia, serif); letter-spacing: -.02em; }
  .hanji-journey p, .research-content p, .research-content li { font: 1rem/1.8 var(--story-body, sans-serif); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
  .product-access { display: inline-block; margin-top: 1rem; padding: .55rem 0; font: .95rem/1.5 var(--story-body, sans-serif); text-decoration: underline; text-decoration-color: #72776a; }
  .product-state { margin: 1rem 0 0; font-size: .95rem; }
  .hanji-journey :global(figure) { margin-block: 1.5rem; }
  .hanji-journey :global(figcaption) { max-width: 88ch; font: .8rem/1.65 var(--story-body, sans-serif); color: var(--theme-text-muted); }
  .hanji-journey :global(.image-link) { padding-bottom: 0 !important; }
  .hanji-journey :global(img), .hanji-journey :global(video) { border-radius: 5px; }
  .detail-spread { display: grid; grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr; align-items: center; gap: clamp(2.5rem, 6vw, 6rem); margin: 4rem auto 0; }
  .detail-copy { max-width: 40ch; }
  .detail-copy p { margin: 1.2rem 0; }
  .connections-section { margin-top: 4rem; }
  .connections-section > h3 { margin-bottom: 2rem; }
  .artifact-paper {
    --theme-bg: #f8f7f4; --theme-text: #343330; --theme-text-muted: #68675e; --theme-border: #d8d8cf;
    --color-bg: var(--theme-bg); --color-text: var(--theme-text); --color-text-muted: var(--theme-text-muted); --color-border: var(--theme-border);
    background: var(--theme-bg); color: var(--theme-text); border-radius: 5px; padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 3rem);
  }
  .artifact-paper :global(figure) { margin: 0; }
  .artifact-paper :global(figcaption) { color: #68675e; }
  .connections-section .implementation-note { margin-top: 1rem; font-size: .85rem; }
  .identity-plate :global(.brand-sheet) { min-height: 240px; grid-template-columns: 120px 1fr; padding: 1rem; gap: 3rem; background: transparent; border: 0; }
  .identity-plate :global(.mark-study) { padding-right: 2rem; gap: .8rem; }
  .identity-plate :global(.mark-study svg) { width: 80px; }
  .identity-plate :global(.wordmark) { font-size: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem); margin: .6rem 0; }
  .palette-plate { margin-top: 2rem; }
  .palette-plate :global(.mode) { --theme-text: var(--ink); --theme-text-muted: var(--ink); }
  .design-note { max-width: 70ch; margin: 1.5rem auto 0; }
  .shortcut-list { margin: 2rem 0 0; }
  .shortcut-list > div { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 1rem; padding: .9rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--theme-border); font: .9rem/1.5 var(--story-body, sans-serif); }
  .shortcut-list dd { margin: 0; }
  .shortcut-list kbd { font: .8rem/1.4 var(--font-mono, monospace); white-space: nowrap; }
  .case-research { border-block: 1px solid var(--theme-border); }
  .case-research > summary { padding: 1.5rem 0; font-size: .95rem; cursor: pointer; }
  .research-content { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 2rem 4rem; padding: 1.5rem 0; }
  .research-content h3 { font-size: 1.8rem; }
  .research-content h4 { font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 500; }
  .research-content p, .research-content li { font-size: .95rem; }
  @media(max-width:1000px) {
    .opening-visual { max-width: 100%; }
    .detail-spread { gap: 2.5rem; grid-template-columns: .9fr 1.1fr; }
  }
  @media(max-width:650px) {
    .hanji-story h3 { font-size: 1.9rem; }
    .hanji-journey p { font-size: 1rem; }
    .detail-spread, .research-content { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1.5rem; }
    .detail-spread { margin-top: 3rem; }
    .detail-copy { max-width: none; }
    .connections-section { margin-top: 3rem; }
    .identity-plate :global(.brand-sheet) { grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr; padding: 0; gap: 1.25rem; min-height: 190px; }
    .identity-plate :global(.mark-study) { padding-right: 1rem; }
    .identity-plate :global(.mark-study svg) { width: 42px; }
  }
</style>
